<!--
  MachineBlocks — SCAD documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.BlockFileStructure
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <name>BlockFileStructure</name>
  <type>scad:BlockFileStructure</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks V3 Block File structure</is>

  <documentation>
    A Block Module is the reusable OpenSCAD module that calls mb_block() (directly or indirectly).
    Naming: mb__&lt;package&gt;__&lt;Class&gt; with package segments separated by double underscores
    (example: mb__com__machineblocks__examples__Cross).
    Signature is always (config, settings).

    A Block File is a self-contained .scad file: Block Module plus customizer variables and a main
    module call. Mandatory section order, each marked with a /* Section Name */ comment:

    Mandatory Header
    Imports
    Customization
    Main Module Call
    Main Module Definition
    Optional Sub Modules
    Optional Helper Modules
    Optional Global Functions

    Header first line inside the comment must be exactly: MachineBlocks.com Block File.
    Required fields: Name, Filename, FQN. Copyright, license, and visit lines are optional.

    Imports: use the library block.scad; include mb_config.scad. Inside modules, always pass the
    config parameter — do not rely on globals for config.

    Customization uses OpenSCAD Customizer tabs and annotations. Hidden section may only bridge
    customizer variables into module arguments — no internal module computations and no
    mb_param_*() calls at file scope.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="scad:ModulePatterns" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — Primitive Wrapper, Simple, and Composite patterns with full-file examples.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:LegacyConversion" relation="SeeAlso">
      Converting V2 machineblock() files into this structure.
    </see>
    <see file="domains/machineblocks/machineblocks-v3-scad-target/runtimes/scad-lib/docs/03_patterns_and_examples.md" relation="DeepDive">
      Extended Block File and customizer rules.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
